  "body": "Give the 3D `Deburr` operation manual edge selection, edge exclusion, a minimum edge angle filter, and a circular hole filter.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/deburr.rs` (`DeburrParams`)\n- `crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs` (`OpParams::Deburr`)\n- `crates/app/src/operation/material_region.rs` (`!selection_drives_region`)\n- `crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs` (`drive_chains`)\n- `crates/motion/src/drilling/recognize.rs` (`drilling::recognize`, `recognize_cross`)\n- `crates/app/src/commands/operation/geometry.rs`, `crates/app/src/project/file.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/`\n\n## What to change\n\n1. Remove `OpType::Deburr` from the `!selection_drives_region` guard so `SrcRef::Selection` drives manual edge chains (`FeatureSel::Chain`). Keep automatic facet crease detection when `SrcRef::Selection` is empty.\n2. Add `exclude_edges: Vec<GeoSel>` (default empty) to `OpParams::Deburr`. Remove picked `FeatureSel::Chain` edges from auto-detected edges.\n3. Add `min_edge_angle_deg: f64` (default `40.0`, matching `CREASE_DEG` in `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature.rs`) to `DeburrParams` and `OpParams::Deburr`. Keep only convex edges with normal bend angle `acos(n1.dot(n2)) >= min_edge_angle_deg`.\n4. Add hole filter fields (`exclude_holes: bool`, `hole_min_diameter: f64`, `hole_max_diameter: f64`). Detect circular holes using `drilling::recognize` and `recognize_cross` (`Hole`, `CrossHole`) and skip hole rims inside that diameter range.\n5. Wire all new fields through `OpParams::Deburr`, `sane.rs`, commands, project file fields (`serde(default)`), MCP `ParamsDto` (`edit` and `pick`), and UI pages (`geo_page.rs`, `mill2d_more_page.rs`).\n\n## Done means\n\n- The user includes or excludes `FeatureSel::Chain` edges, sets `min_edge_angle_deg`, and skips circular holes inside a diameter range in both UI and MCP.\n- Auto-detection skips convex creases whose normal bend angle is below `min_edge_angle_deg`.\n- Motion and app tests pin chain selection, chain exclusion, angle filtering, hole diameter filtering, and project round-trip.\n\nPart of #1827\n",
